{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "id": "dendera-light",
  "locale": "en",
  "source": {
    "filename": "Dendera_Light_Interaktif_Dosya.html",
    "sha256": "4bc297cc500f4e79abaca7d2868374fd4c0b4c6f516fb41236d18010d7ab562f",
    "revision": "2026-10-06"
  },
  "editorial": {
    "translationState": "editorial-translation",
    "independentlyReviewed": false,
    "sourceLocale": "tr",
    "sourceRevision": "2026-10-06",
    "sourceContentSha256": "7b87fba78263a25e326f062b2fbacc3448b3c844f44b1f8addb8a888189c2650"
  },
  "sections": [
    {
      "tag": "section",
      "attrs": {
        "id": "ozet"
      },
      "children": [
        "\n",
        {
          "tag": "h2",
          "attrs": {},
          "children": [
            "The case in 60 seconds"
          ]
        },
        "\n",
        {
          "tag": "div",
          "attrs": {
            "class": "card emphasis"
          },
          "children": [
            "\n",
            {
              "tag": "p",
              "attrs": {
                "class": "quote"
              },
              "children": [
                "\nThe Dendera “bulbs” do not provide independent evidence of electrical technology. The reliefs' own inscriptions and the temple's theology explain the scene in terms of ",
                {
                  "tag": "b",
                  "attrs": {},
                  "children": [
                    "Harsomtus, the serpent-shaped god born from the lotus."
                  ]
                },
                " That is its religious context.\n"
              ]
            },
            "\n",
            {
              "tag": "p",
              "attrs": {},
              "children": [
                "\nSome reliefs in the crypts of the Temple of Hathor at Dendera resemble a large glass light bulb to a modern observer. A serpent appears inside the oval shape, with a lotus flower beneath, and a ",
                {
                  "tag": "b",
                  "attrs": {},
                  "children": [
                    "djed"
                  ]
                },
                " pillar and ritual figures beside it.\n"
              ]
            },
            "\n",
            {
              "tag": "p",
              "attrs": {},
              "children": [
                "\nMajor Egyptological publications on Dendera read these as ",
                {
                  "tag": "b",
                  "attrs": {},
                  "children": [
                    "cosmogonic and cultic scenes"
                  ]
                },
                " depicting Harsomtus's birth from the lotus, rather than electrical circuits. Even the title of Wolfgang Waitkus's study directly examining this iconography refers to “Harsomtus's birth from the flower”.\n"
              ]
            },
            "\n",
            {
              "tag": "p",
              "attrs": {},
              "children": [
                "\nThe electrical theory's greatest difficulty is its lack of context: no ",
                {
                  "tag": "b",
                  "attrs": {},
                  "children": [
                    "wires, conductive installations, generators, switches, bulb remains, glass-vacuum technology or electrically operated devices"
                  ]
                },
                " supporting such a system have been found in ancient Egypt.\n"
              ]
            },
            "\n"
          ]
        },
        "\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "tag": "section",
      "attrs": {
        "id": "iddia"
      },
      "children": [
        "\n",
        {
          "tag": "h2",
          "attrs": {},
          "children": [
            "The claim"
          ]
        },
        "\n",
        {
          "tag": "div",
          "attrs": {
            "class": "card"
          },
          "children": [
            "\n",
            {
              "tag": "p",
              "attrs": {
                "class": "quote"
              },
              "children": [
                "\n“The Dendera relief clearly depicts a giant electric light bulb. The serpent is the filament, the djed pillar an insulator and the extending line a cable. Ancient Egyptians must therefore have lit their temples with electricity.”\n"
              ]
            },
            "\n",
            {
              "tag": "p",
              "attrs": {},
              "children": [
                "\nThe interpretation's appeal comes from visual resemblance. In archaeology, however, resemblance to a modern device does not establish that an object depicts that device. Context must take priority, especially when hieroglyphs beside the scene explain what it represents.\n"
              ]
            },
            "\n"
          ]
        },
        "\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "tag": "section",
      "attrs": {
        "id": "gercekler"
      },
      "children": [
        "\n",
        {
          "tag": "h2",
          "attrs": {},
          "children": [
            "What we know"
          ]
        },
        "\n",
        {
          "tag": "div",
          "attrs": {
            "class": "grid"
          },
          "children": [
            "\n",
            {
              "tag": "div",
              "attrs": {
                "class": "fact"
              },
              "children": [
                {
                  "tag": "b",
                  "attrs": {},
                  "children": [
                    "The reliefs are real"
                  ]
                },
                "The scenes belong to the Temple of Hathor's decorative programme and occur in its crypts."
              ]
            },
            "\n",
            {
              "tag": "div",
              "attrs": {
                "class": "fact"
              },
              "children": [
                {
                  "tag": "b",
                  "attrs": {},
                  "children": [
                    "The temple is a late-period building"
                  ]
                },
                "The present Temple of Hathor was largely completed in the Ptolemaic and Roman periods; its decorative programme is extensive and theologically complex."
              ]
            },
            "\n",
            {
              "tag": "div",
              "attrs": {
                "class": "fact"
              },
              "children": [
                {
                  "tag": "b",
                  "attrs": {},
                  "children": [
                    "The crypts were sacred storerooms"
                  ]
                },
                "Dendera has 11 decorated crypts associated with cult objects, statues and ritual materials."
              ]
            },
            "\n",
            {
              "tag": "div",
              "attrs": {
                "class": "fact"
              },
              "children": [
                {
                  "tag": "b",
                  "attrs": {},
                  "children": [
                    "The thing inside the “bulb” is identified as a serpent"
                  ]
                },
                "Dendera texts associate Harsomtus with the lotus and serpent form."
              ]
            },
            "\n",
            {
              "tag": "div",
              "attrs": {
                "class": "fact"
              },
              "children": [
                {
                  "tag": "b",
                  "attrs": {},
                  "children": [
                    "The djed is not an electrical insulator"
                  ]
                },
                "The djed is a very ancient sacred symbol in Egyptian iconography, associated with Osiris and endurance/stability."
              ]
            },
            "\n",
            {
              "tag": "div",
              "attrs": {
                "class": "fact"
              },
              "children": [
                {
                  "tag": "b",
                  "attrs": {},
                  "children": [
                    "No electrical infrastructure"
                  ]
                },
                "Egyptian archaeology has revealed no physical technological chain connecting the Dendera reliefs to a real electrical system."
              ]
            },
            "\n"
          ]
        },
        "\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "tag": "section",
      "attrs": {
        "id": "kanitlar"
      },
      "children": [
        "\n",
        {
          "tag": "h2",
          "attrs": {},
          "children": [
            "The evidence"
          ]
        },
        "\n\n",
        {
          "tag": "h3",
          "attrs": {},
          "children": [
            "1 — The scene's own text gives a mythological context"
          ]
        },
        "\n",
        {
          "tag": "div",
          "attrs": {
            "class": "card"
          },
          "children": [
            "\n",
            {
              "tag": "p",
              "attrs": {},
              "children": [
                "\nIn Dendera research, the cult of Harsomtus is directly associated with the lotus. Publications on Dendera's sacred geography describe the lotus as the serpent's cradle in a creation context. The serpent inside the oval is therefore an element of Egyptian religious iconography before it is a modern “filament”.\n"
              ]
            },
            "\n",
            {
              "tag": "span",
              "attrs": {
                "class": "pill green"
              },
              "children": [
                "Direct iconographic context"
              ]
            },
            "\n"
          ]
        },
        "\n\n",
        {
          "tag": "h3",
          "attrs": {},
          "children": [
            "2 — The scene belongs to a comprehensive theological programme"
          ]
        },
        "\n",
        {
          "tag": "div",
          "attrs": {
            "class": "card"
          },
          "children": [
            "\n",
            {
              "tag": "p",
              "attrs": {},
              "children": [
                "\nDendera is not a building of unrelated pictures. Researchers describe a complex theological programme in which writing, wordplay, sacred symbols and architectural space work together. Barbara Richter's study of Hathor's theology shows how Dendera scribes used visual and hieroglyphic elements to produce layered meanings.\n"
              ]
            },
            "\n",
            {
              "tag": "span",
              "attrs": {
                "class": "pill green"
              },
              "children": [
                "The context weakens a “technical drawing” interpretation"
              ]
            },
            "\n"
          ]
        },
        "\n\n",
        {
          "tag": "h3",
          "attrs": {},
          "children": [
            "3 — Dendera's crypts were not “secret laboratories”"
          ]
        },
        "\n",
        {
          "tag": "div",
          "attrs": {
            "class": "card"
          },
          "children": [
            "\n",
            {
              "tag": "p",
              "attrs": {},
              "children": [
                "\nRecent Dendera publications identify 11 decorated crypts within the complex ritual-theological system. Storing statues, cult objects and ritual materials in crypts during the Ptolemaic period is consistent with Egyptian temple practice.\n"
              ]
            },
            "\n",
            {
              "tag": "span",
              "attrs": {
                "class": "pill green"
              },
              "children": [
                "A known temple function"
              ]
            },
            "\n"
          ]
        },
        "\n\n",
        {
          "tag": "h3",
          "attrs": {},
          "children": [
            "4 — Nothing establishes that the line called a “cable” is electrical"
          ]
        },
        "\n",
        {
          "tag": "div",
          "attrs": {
            "class": "card"
          },
          "children": [
            "\n",
            {
              "tag": "p",
              "attrs": {},
              "children": [
                "\nThe bulb theory interprets an element extending from the lotus or oval as an electric cable. Yet the scene contains no inscription specifying voltage, conductors, connections or a technical function. The same symbols integrate meaningfully with the mythological scene's other elements.\n"
              ]
            },
            "\n",
            {
              "tag": "span",
              "attrs": {
                "class": "pill red"
              },
              "children": [
                "No evidence for the electrical interpretation"
              ]
            },
            "\n"
          ]
        },
        "\n\n",
        {
          "tag": "h3",
          "attrs": {},
          "children": [
            "5 — Real bulb technology would require much more than “one picture”"
          ]
        },
        "\n",
        {
          "tag": "div",
          "attrs": {
            "class": "card"
          },
          "children": [
            "\n",
            {
              "tag": "p",
              "attrs": {},
              "children": [
                "\nElectrical lighting requires a power source, conductive connections, electrodes/filaments, controlled gas or vacuum, suitable glassmaking and a technical tradition enabling repeated use. Such material culture has not emerged in Egyptian archaeology.\n"
              ]
            },
            "\n",
            {
              "tag": "span",
              "attrs": {
                "class": "pill green"
              },
              "children": [
                "The technological chain is entirely missing"
              ]
            },
            "\n"
          ]
        },
        "\n\n",
        {
          "tag": "h3",
          "attrs": {},
          "children": [
            "6 — The “no torch soot” argument is insufficient"
          ]
        },
        "\n",
        {
          "tag": "div",
          "attrs": {
            "class": "card"
          },
          "children": [
            "\n",
            {
              "tag": "p",
              "attrs": {},
              "children": [
                "\nAdvocates of Dendera Light often say “there is no soot in the crypts, so they had electricity”. That conclusion is not necessary. Oil lamps, controlled lighting, short periods of work, surface cleaning and other lighting methods are possible in ancient buildings. “No soot was observed” does not, by itself, demonstrate electricity.\n"
              ]
            },
            "\n",
            {
              "tag": "span",
              "attrs": {
                "class": "pill yellow"
              },
              "children": [
                "An unwarranted conclusion from negative evidence"
              ]
            },
            "\n"
          ]
        },
        "\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "tag": "section",
      "attrs": {
        "id": "teoriler"
      },
      "children": [
        "\n",
        {
          "tag": "h2",
          "attrs": {},
          "children": [
            "Theories"
          ]
        },
        "\n\n",
        {
          "tag": "details",
          "attrs": {},
          "children": [
            "\n",
            {
              "tag": "summary",
              "attrs": {},
              "children": [
                "Theory A — A ritual/cosmogonic scene of Harsomtus's birth from the lotus"
              ]
            },
            "\n",
            {
              "tag": "div",
              "attrs": {
                "class": "inside"
              },
              "children": [
                "\n",
                {
                  "tag": "p",
                  "attrs": {},
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "tag": "b",
                      "attrs": {},
                      "children": [
                        "Strength:"
                      ]
                    },
                    " Directly consistent with Dendera's inscriptions, temple theology, lotus-serpent iconography and the cult of Harsomtus. This is the main explanation in Egyptological literature."
                  ]
                },
                "\n",
                {
                  "tag": "p",
                  "attrs": {},
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "tag": "b",
                      "attrs": {},
                      "children": [
                        "Weakness:"
                      ]
                    },
                    " Ptolemaic symbolism at Dendera is multilayered; a single modern sentence may not exhaust every iconographic detail."
                  ]
                },
                "\n"
              ]
            },
            "\n"
          ]
        },
        "\n\n",
        {
          "tag": "details",
          "attrs": {},
          "children": [
            "\n",
            {
              "tag": "summary",
              "attrs": {},
              "children": [
                "Theory B — A symbolic “cosmic birth / solar creation” scene"
              ]
            },
            "\n",
            {
              "tag": "div",
              "attrs": {
                "class": "inside"
              },
              "children": [
                "\n",
                {
                  "tag": "p",
                  "attrs": {},
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "tag": "b",
                      "attrs": {},
                      "children": [
                        "Strength:"
                      ]
                    },
                    " Lotus, serpent, djed and sacred barque/supporting elements are familiar Egyptian cosmogonic motifs. Connections between Harsomtus, Horus and solar creation are strong at Dendera."
                  ]
                },
                "\n",
                {
                  "tag": "p",
                  "attrs": {},
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "tag": "b",
                      "attrs": {},
                      "children": [
                        "Weakness:"
                      ]
                    },
                    " Ptolemaic hieroglyphs are exceptionally dense and rich in wordplay; detailed interpretation requires specialist knowledge."
                  ]
                },
                "\n"
              ]
            },
            "\n"
          ]
        },
        "\n\n",
        {
          "tag": "details",
          "attrs": {},
          "children": [
            "\n",
            {
              "tag": "summary",
              "attrs": {},
              "children": [
                "Theory C — An electric light bulb / high-voltage device"
              ]
            },
            "\n",
            {
              "tag": "div",
              "attrs": {
                "class": "inside"
              },
              "children": [
                "\n",
                {
                  "tag": "p",
                  "attrs": {},
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "tag": "b",
                      "attrs": {},
                      "children": [
                        "Strength:"
                      ]
                    },
                    " It can be made to look strikingly similar to a modern bulb: the serpent as “filament”, oval as “glass” and djed as “insulator”."
                  ]
                },
                "\n",
                {
                  "tag": "p",
                  "attrs": {},
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "tag": "b",
                      "attrs": {},
                      "children": [
                        "Weakness:"
                      ]
                    },
                    " These matches project modern technology backwards. The hieroglyphs do not describe the elements electrically, and the necessary archaeological technological chain is entirely absent."
                  ]
                },
                "\n"
              ]
            },
            "\n"
          ]
        },
        "\n\n",
        {
          "tag": "details",
          "attrs": {},
          "children": [
            "\n",
            {
              "tag": "summary",
              "attrs": {},
              "children": [
                "Theory D — The Baghdad Battery and Dendera bulb formed an electrical system together"
              ]
            },
            "\n",
            {
              "tag": "div",
              "attrs": {
                "class": "inside"
              },
              "children": [
                "\n",
                {
                  "tag": "p",
                  "attrs": {},
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "tag": "b",
                      "attrs": {},
                      "children": [
                        "Strength:"
                      ]
                    },
                    " It combines two mysteries into one explanation in popular accounts."
                  ]
                },
                "\n",
                {
                  "tag": "p",
                  "attrs": {},
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "tag": "b",
                      "attrs": {},
                      "children": [
                        "Weakness:"
                      ]
                    },
                    " There is no direct connection across geography, period, context or the evidence chain. Even the Baghdad Battery's use as a battery has not been established."
                  ]
                },
                "\n"
              ]
            },
            "\n"
          ]
        },
        "\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "tag": "section",
      "attrs": {
        "id": "viral"
      },
      "children": [
        "\n",
        {
          "tag": "h2",
          "attrs": {},
          "children": [
            "Viral claims: are they true?"
          ]
        },
        "\n",
        {
          "tag": "table",
          "attrs": {},
          "children": [
            "\n",
            {
              "tag": "thead",
              "attrs": {},
              "children": [
                {
                  "tag": "tr",
                  "attrs": {},
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "tag": "th",
                      "attrs": {},
                      "children": [
                        "Claim"
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "tag": "th",
                      "attrs": {},
                      "children": [
                        "Assessment"
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "tag": "th",
                      "attrs": {},
                      "children": [
                        "Why?"
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            "\n",
            {
              "tag": "tbody",
              "attrs": {},
              "children": [
                "\n",
                {
                  "tag": "tr",
                  "attrs": {},
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "tag": "td",
                      "attrs": {},
                      "children": [
                        "“The relief clearly shows an electric bulb.”"
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "tag": "td",
                      "attrs": {},
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "tag": "span",
                          "attrs": {
                            "class": "pill red"
                          },
                          "children": [
                            "A modern analogy"
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "tag": "td",
                      "attrs": {},
                      "children": [
                        "Its own textual and religious context concerns Harsomtus, the lotus and cosmogony."
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                },
                "\n",
                {
                  "tag": "tr",
                  "attrs": {},
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "tag": "td",
                      "attrs": {},
                      "children": [
                        "“The serpent is a filament.”"
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "tag": "td",
                      "attrs": {},
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "tag": "span",
                          "attrs": {
                            "class": "pill red"
                          },
                          "children": [
                            "No evidence"
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "tag": "td",
                      "attrs": {},
                      "children": [
                        "The serpent is already a sacred, creation-related motif in Egyptian mythology."
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                },
                "\n",
                {
                  "tag": "tr",
                  "attrs": {},
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "tag": "td",
                      "attrs": {},
                      "children": [
                        "“The djed pillar is an electrical insulator.”"
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "tag": "td",
                      "attrs": {},
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "tag": "span",
                          "attrs": {
                            "class": "pill red"
                          },
                          "children": [
                            "Incorrect context"
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "tag": "td",
                      "attrs": {},
                      "children": [
                        "The djed is an Osiris/stability symbol known from much earlier periods."
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                },
                "\n",
                {
                  "tag": "tr",
                  "attrs": {},
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "tag": "td",
                      "attrs": {},
                      "children": [
                        "“There is no soot anywhere in the temple.”"
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "tag": "td",
                      "attrs": {},
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "tag": "span",
                          "attrs": {
                            "class": "pill yellow"
                          },
                          "children": [
                            "An overgeneralisation"
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "tag": "td",
                      "attrs": {},
                      "children": [
                        "The absence of heavy soot in a space does not establish electrical technology."
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                },
                "\n",
                {
                  "tag": "tr",
                  "attrs": {},
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "tag": "td",
                      "attrs": {},
                      "children": [
                        "“Pyramid and temple interiors stayed clean because Egyptians used electricity.”"
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "tag": "td",
                      "attrs": {},
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "tag": "span",
                          "attrs": {
                            "class": "pill red"
                          },
                          "children": [
                            "No evidence"
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "tag": "td",
                      "attrs": {},
                      "children": [
                        "Electrical infrastructure, devices or textual descriptions have not been found."
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                },
                "\n",
                {
                  "tag": "tr",
                  "attrs": {},
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "tag": "td",
                      "attrs": {},
                      "children": [
                        "“The hieroglyphs describe an electrical device.”"
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "tag": "td",
                      "attrs": {},
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "tag": "span",
                          "attrs": {
                            "class": "pill red"
                          },
                          "children": [
                            "False"
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "tag": "td",
                      "attrs": {},
                      "children": [
                        "Egyptological readings yield divine and ritual expressions, not descriptions of voltage, current or technical devices."
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                },
                "\n",
                {
                  "tag": "tr",
                  "attrs": {},
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "tag": "td",
                      "attrs": {},
                      "children": [
                        "“Mainstream archaeology is concealing this knowledge.”"
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "tag": "td",
                      "attrs": {},
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "tag": "span",
                          "attrs": {
                            "class": "pill red"
                          },
                          "children": [
                            "No evidence"
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "tag": "td",
                      "attrs": {},
                      "children": [
                        "Dendera's reliefs, inscriptions and crypts have been extensively published."
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                },
                "\n"
              ]
            },
            "\n"
          ]
        },
        "\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "tag": "section",
      "attrs": {
        "id": "bilinmeyen"
      },
      "children": [
        "\n",
        {
          "tag": "h2",
          "attrs": {},
          "children": [
            "What remains unknown"
          ]
        },
        "\n",
        {
          "tag": "div",
          "attrs": {
            "class": "grid"
          },
          "children": [
            "\n",
            {
              "tag": "div",
              "attrs": {
                "class": "fact"
              },
              "children": [
                {
                  "tag": "b",
                  "attrs": {},
                  "children": [
                    "The nuance of every iconographic detail"
                  ]
                },
                "Ptolemaic hieroglyphic and visual wordplay is multilayered; specific functions of different cult objects remain subjects for specialist debate."
              ]
            },
            "\n",
            {
              "tag": "div",
              "attrs": {
                "class": "fact"
              },
              "children": [
                {
                  "tag": "b",
                  "attrs": {},
                  "children": [
                    "The full practice of the crypt rituals"
                  ]
                },
                "The texts tell us much, but precisely how every ritual was performed is not completely known."
              ]
            },
            "\n",
            {
              "tag": "div",
              "attrs": {
                "class": "fact"
              },
              "children": [
                {
                  "tag": "b",
                  "attrs": {},
                  "children": [
                    "The physical form of particular cult objects"
                  ]
                },
                "The actual three-dimensional counterparts of some sacred objects represented in the reliefs may be lost."
              ]
            },
            "\n",
            {
              "tag": "div",
              "attrs": {
                "class": "fact"
              },
              "children": [
                {
                  "tag": "b",
                  "attrs": {},
                  "children": [
                    "Why is the “bulb resemblance” so powerful?"
                  ]
                },
                "This is more a question of perception than a scientific mystery: eyes familiar with modern objects readily recognise modern forms in ancient symbols."
              ]
            },
            "\n"
          ]
        },
        "\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "tag": "section",
      "attrs": {
        "id": "degerlendirme"
      },
      "children": [
        "\n",
        {
          "tag": "h2",
          "attrs": {},
          "children": [
            "My assessment"
          ]
        },
        "\n",
        {
          "tag": "div",
          "attrs": {
            "class": "card emphasis"
          },
          "children": [
            "\n",
            {
              "tag": "p",
              "attrs": {
                "class": "verdict"
              },
              "children": [
                "🟢 Dendera Light is largely a mystery created by analogy with modern technology."
              ]
            },
            "\n",
            {
              "tag": "p",
              "attrs": {},
              "children": [
                "\nThis is one of the cases most similar to the Baigong Pipes. Looking at the image first makes “light bulb” an easy label; reading the inscriptions, temple context and Egyptian iconography then reveals that the same shape already makes sense within its own culture.\n"
              ]
            },
            "\n",
            {
              "tag": "p",
              "attrs": {},
              "children": [
                "\nThe electrical hypothesis's main difficulty is its matching of individual symbols to modern device components:\n",
                {
                  "tag": "b",
                  "attrs": {},
                  "children": [
                    "serpent = filament, djed = insulator, lotus = socket, line = cable."
                  ]
                },
                "\nEach already exists as a symbol in Egyptian religion independently of electricity.\n"
              ]
            },
            "\n",
            {
              "tag": "p",
              "attrs": {},
              "children": [
                "\nIf electrical technology really had been used, we would expect more than one relief: an entire material technological ecosystem. No such ecosystem is currently present.\n"
              ]
            },
            "\n",
            {
              "tag": "p",
              "attrs": {},
              "children": [
                "\nThe strongest explanation is therefore that the Dendera scenes represent ",
                {
                  "tag": "b",
                  "attrs": {},
                  "children": [
                    "Harsomtus's emergence from the lotus and a theology of creation/renewal."
                  ]
                },
                " That is what the context supports.\n"
              ]
            },
            "\n"
          ]
        },
        "\n",
        {
          "tag": "div",
          "attrs": {
            "class": "callout"
          },
          "children": [
            "\n",
            {
              "tag": "b",
              "attrs": {},
              "children": [
                "Status in this series:"
              ]
            },
            " 🟢 ",
            {
              "tag": "b",
              "attrs": {},
              "children": [
                "Largely explained."
              ]
            },
            {
              "tag": "br",
              "attrs": {},
              "children": []
            },
            "\nDetailed theological interpretation remains a specialist subject, but there is no archaeological evidence supporting an “ancient electric bulb”.\n"
          ]
        },
        "\n"
      ]
    },
